#: ../../source/docs/common-betafpvf405.rst:203
#: bf38990ed950408696daa0e106cfbedd
msgid "Connecting a GPS/Compass module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-betafpvf405.rst:205
#: 6c7919ef6cc0484c96d64930bee13c8f
msgid "This board does not include a GPS and compass so an :ref:`external GPS <common-positioning-landing-page>` can be connected to allow operation of position holding/tracking modes (ie LOITER,etc.). However, only the AIO has the ability to disconnect its ELRS module to provide the required access to the UART3 RX/TX pins to attach an I2C compass. This also requires special firmware (see below) be installed to convert these pins from UART use to I2C use with RX3 becoming SDA and TX3 becoming SCL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-betafpvf405.rst:207
#: 35120c65acfc42d78dd861615ee74888
msgid "since a compass cannot be normally attached, only ACRO, STABILIZE, and ALTHOLD (if the unit has a BARO) modes are recommended. GSF (:ref:`common-compassless`)can be used, but requires pre-flight actions to converge it before taking off, and it is susceptible to failures in flight."
msgstr ""

